  "track.debugging.preset.loop": "Debugging · guess and patch, or reproduce and narrow down",
  "track.debugging.m.loop.title": "A crash that happens \"sometimes\" on the booking details screen",
  "track.debugging.m.loop.overview": "The ClinicBook booking details screen crashes now and then. Way 1 guesses the cause and patches it straight away, three times. Way 2 follows the debugging loop: reproduce, narrow down, form a hypothesis and test it, fix and lock it with a test. Both are tried on the same 8 usage scenarios; each scenario ends normally, in a crash, or on a blank screen.",
  "track.debugging.m.loop.wrapup": "Guessing and patching lowers the crash count, but the bug stays: one patch only avoids one path to it, the next hides it as a blank screen. Following the debugging loop shows that all 4 crashing scenarios share one thing, the screen being recreated, so one fix in one place is enough, and a test keeps the bug from coming back.",
  "track.debugging.m.loop.simp.1": "The 8 usage scenarios are the site's; a real bug may need more scenarios and several runs before it reproduces.",
  "track.debugging.m.loop.simp.2": "Each scenario's result (normal, crash, blank) is really computed in JavaScript from two things: whether the scenario recreates the screen, and which patch is applied. The Kotlin code is illustrative.",
  "track.debugging.m.loop.ctl.hint": "Pick a way of debugging and walk the four steps; watch the scenario table change with each patch.",
