  "track.debugging.m.loop.known.yes": "yes",
  "track.debugging.cap.loop": "The four stations of the debugging loop; a wrong hypothesis goes back to reproducing or narrowing down, a right one exits to the last station: fix and lock with a test.",
  "track.debugging.m.loop.s.guess.s1.title": "Guess 1: rotation causes it, so lock the screen to portrait",
  "track.debugging.m.loop.s.guess.s1.explain": "Someone once saw a crash after rotating the phone, so release 1.4.1 locks the screen to portrait. Crashes drop from 4 to 3 of the 8 scenarios: switching to dark theme, changing the language, and returning after the system has killed the process still crash.",
  "track.debugging.m.loop.ev.guess.s1": "Guess 1: rotation causes it, so lock the screen to portrait",
  "track.debugging.m.loop.s.guess.s2.title": "Guess 2: add a check so it stops crashing",
  "track.debugging.m.loop.s.guess.s2.explain": "The stack trace says booking was never initialised, so release 1.4.2 adds if (!::booking.isInitialized) return. No crash is left, but those 3 scenarios now end on a blank screen: the bug is still there, it is just quiet.",
  "track.debugging.m.loop.ev.guess.s2": "Guess 2: add a check so it stops crashing",
  "track.debugging.m.loop.s.guess.s3.title": "Users report: the details screen is empty",
  "track.debugging.m.loop.s.guess.s3.explain": "One-star reviews say \"tapping a booking shows nothing\". There is no crash in the reports, so there is no stack trace to follow either. A hidden bug is harder to find than a crashing one.",
  "track.debugging.m.loop.ev.guess.s3": "Users report: the details screen is empty",
  "track.debugging.m.loop.s.guess.s4.title": "Three releases, and the cause is still unknown",
  "track.debugging.m.loop.s.guess.s4.explain": "Release 1.4.3 guesses once more. After three releases the team still cannot answer \"when does the bug happen\", so it cannot tell which fix is enough. Every guess is a bet placed on real users.",
  "track.debugging.m.loop.ev.guess.s4": "Three releases, and the cause is still unknown",
  "track.debugging.m.loop.s.method.s1.title": "Reproduce: run all 8 scenarios on a dev device",
  "track.debugging.m.loop.s.method.s1.explain": "Instead of guessing, try the 8 usage scenarios one by one on a debug build. It crashes exactly 4 times, in scenarios 2, 4, 6 and 7, and every time. A bug that reproduces reliably is one whose fix can be checked.",
  "track.debugging.m.loop.ev.method.s1": "Reproduce: run all 8 scenarios on a dev device",
  "track.debugging.m.loop.s.method.s2.title": "Narrow down: what the four crashing scenarios share",
  "track.debugging.m.loop.s.method.s2.explain": "Rotating, switching to dark theme, changing the language, and returning after the process was killed all recreate the Activity and the Fragment. The four scenarios that do not crash do not. The stack trace points at the same line every time: reading booking in onViewCreated.",
  "track.debugging.m.loop.ev.method.s2": "Narrow down: what the four crashing scenarios share",
  "track.debugging.m.loop.s.method.s3.title": "Hypothesis and test: the data is only set through a setter",
  "track.debugging.m.loop.s.method.s3.explain": "Hypothesis: the list screen hands booking to the Fragment through a setter; when the system recreates the Fragment on its own, nobody calls the setter again. Prediction: it crashes if and only if the screen is recreated. The result matches all 8 scenarios, including the 4 that do not crash.",
  "track.debugging.m.loop.ev.method.s3": "Hypothesis and test: the data is only set through a setter",
  "track.debugging.m.loop.s.method.s4.title": "Fix one place, lock it with a test",
  "track.debugging.m.loop.s.method.s4.explain": "Pass the booking id in the Fragment's arguments (saved and handed back by the system on recreation) and load booking from that id. All 8 scenarios end normally, with no blank screen. A test that recreates the screen and checks that the patient name still shows keeps the bug from coming back.",
  "track.debugging.m.loop.ev.method.s4": "Fix one place, lock it with a test",
  "track.debugging.m.loop.co.try": "Reading tip: each table row is a usage scenario; the last column is the result with the current patch. Count the red cells (crash) and the amber cells (blank screen) after each step.",
  "track.debugging.m.loop.co.guess.s2": "A patch that removes the symptom has not necessarily fixed the cause. Here the check only turns a crash into a blank screen.",
  "track.debugging.m.loop.co.guess.s3": "A crash has a stack trace and is collected by Play Console or Crashlytics; a blank screen is not. Hiding the bug removes the very trail needed to find it. [[src:ad-bug-report]]",
  "track.debugging.m.loop.co.guess.s4": "The question to answer before fixing: \"when does the bug happen, and when does it not\". Until that is answered, nobody knows whether a fix is enough.",
  "track.debugging.m.loop.co.method.s1": "Scenario 6 uses adb to imitate the system killing the process: send the app to the background, run adb shell am kill with the package name, then reopen the app. am kill only kills a process that is safe to kill, such as an app in the background. [[src:ad-adb]]",
  "track.debugging.m.loop.co.method.s2": "Comparing the crashing scenarios with the ones that do not crash matters just as much: a shared trait only means something if it is absent from the other group.",
  "track.debugging.m.loop.co.method.s3": "A good hypothesis makes a testable prediction, including \"this one will not crash\". If one scenario does not match, the hypothesis is wrong and we go round the loop again.",
  "track.debugging.m.loop.co.method.s4": "The test must be red before the fix and green after it; only then is it sure to check this bug. Reproducing bugs as tests and bisecting the commit history are covered in \"Methodical debugging: reproduce and bisect\" in the Clean Code and Craft track.",
  "track.debugging.vz.tab.loop": "Debugging loop and scenario table",
