  "track.debugging.cap.bp": "The breakpoint stops the report thread; a red box marks a problem: too many stops, or the sync thread frozen too and the session lost.",
  "track.debugging.m.bp.s.plain.s1.title": "A plain breakpoint in the loop: it stops at booking 0",
  "track.debugging.m.bp.s.plain.s1.explain": "The breakpoint sits on the line that adds the fee. It stops on the very first iteration, i = 0, fee 200,000 VND, nothing wrong. A plain breakpoint stops every time execution passes that line.",
  "track.debugging.m.bp.ev.plain.s1": "A plain breakpoint in the loop: it stops at booking 0",
  "track.debugging.m.bp.s.plain.s2.title": "Resume 347 times to reach the bad booking",
  "track.debugging.m.bp.s.plain.s2.explain": "The bad booking is i = 347, so the app stops 348 times and you press resume 347 times. This is exactly why people give up on the debugger and go back to adding a Log and rebuilding.",
  "track.debugging.m.bp.ev.plain.s2": "Resume 347 times to reach the bad booking",
  "track.debugging.m.bp.s.plain.s3.title": "Thirty seconds on the variables: the sync thread freezes too, the server ends the session",
  "track.debugging.m.bp.s.plain.s3.explain": "By default a breakpoint suspends every thread (Suspend All). During the 30 seconds you read the variables, the sync thread sends no heartbeat; after 10 seconds the server ends the session. On resuming, the app meets a second error caused by the debugging itself.",
  "track.debugging.m.bp.ev.plain.s3": "Thirty seconds on the variables: the sync thread freezes too, the server ends the session",
  "track.debugging.m.bp.s.cond.s1.title": "Condition fee < 0: run straight past the normal bookings",
  "track.debugging.m.bp.s.cond.s1.explain": "A conditional breakpoint stops only when its expression is true. You do not need to know which booking is bad: put the condition on the symptom, a negative fee. The first 347 bookings run through without a stop.",
  "track.debugging.m.bp.ev.cond.s1": "Condition fee < 0: run straight past the normal bookings",
  "track.debugging.m.bp.s.cond.s2.title": "One stop, at booking 347: a 120% discount",
  "track.debugging.m.bp.s.cond.s2.explain": "The app stops exactly once. The variables show base = 200,000 and discountPercent = 120, so fee = −40,000. The cause is plain: the discount was never checked where it was entered.",
  "track.debugging.m.bp.ev.cond.s2": "One stop, at booking 347: a 120% discount",
  "track.debugging.m.bp.s.cond.s3.title": "Still suspending all threads: 30 seconds of looking, the session ends",
  "track.debugging.m.bp.s.cond.s3.explain": "Only one stop, but the policy is still Suspend All. While you read the variables, the sync thread is frozen for 30 seconds and the server ends the session. Fewer stops is not enough; you also choose which threads stop.",
  "track.debugging.m.bp.ev.cond.s3": "Still suspending all threads: 30 seconds of looking, the session ends",
  "track.debugging.m.bp.s.thread.s1.title": "The same condition, but suspend only the thread that hits it",
  "track.debugging.m.bp.s.thread.s1.explain": "Suspend Thread policy: when the report thread hits the breakpoint, only that thread stops. The other threads keep running as if nothing happened.",
  "track.debugging.m.bp.ev.thread.s1": "The same condition, but suspend only the thread that hits it",
  "track.debugging.m.bp.s.thread.s2.title": "One stop at booking 347; the sync thread keeps running",
  "track.debugging.m.bp.s.thread.s2.explain": "The variables are exactly as before: discountPercent = 120. The difference is the lower lane: the sync thread still sends a heartbeat every second.",
  "track.debugging.m.bp.ev.thread.s2": "One stop at booking 347; the sync thread keeps running",
  "track.debugging.m.bp.s.thread.s3.title": "Thirty seconds of looking, the sync session is still alive",
  "track.debugging.m.bp.s.thread.s3.explain": "No heartbeat is missed and the server keeps the session. The trade-off: other threads can still change data while you look, so a shared value may differ between two looks.",
  "track.debugging.m.bp.ev.thread.s3": "Thirty seconds of looking, the sync session is still alive",
  "track.debugging.m.bp.s.logbp.s1.title": "A non-suspending breakpoint: log \"i, fee\" on every pass",
  "track.debugging.m.bp.s.logbp.s1.explain": "Untick Suspend and turn on \"Evaluate and log\" with the expression \"i=$i fee=$fee\". The app never stops; each pass over the line writes one line. No Log call is added to the code.",
  "track.debugging.m.bp.ev.logbp.s1": "A non-suspending breakpoint: log \"i, fee\" on every pass",
  "track.debugging.m.bp.s.logbp.s2.title": "500 log lines; filtering for a negative fee leaves one: i = 347",
  "track.debugging.m.bp.s.logbp.s2.explain": "Filtering for a negative fee leaves exactly one line, i = 347, fee = −40,000. The sync thread is never stopped.",
  "track.debugging.m.bp.ev.logbp.s2": "500 log lines; filtering for a negative fee leaves one: i = 347",
  "track.debugging.m.bp.s.logbp.s3.title": "Want another variable: edit the expression, no rebuild",
  "track.debugging.m.bp.s.logbp.s3.explain": "To print discountPercent too, just edit the breakpoint's expression and run the loop again. Adding Log.d to the code means a rebuild and reinstall for every change, and it is easy to forget to remove before release.",
  "track.debugging.m.bp.ev.logbp.s3": "Want another variable: edit the expression, no rebuild",
  "track.debugging.m.bp.co.try": "Reading tip: the upper lane is the report thread going through 500 bookings, a red mark is where the app stops; the lower lane is the sync thread, each dot a heartbeat to the server. A red break in the lower lane is when the sync thread was frozen too.",
  "track.debugging.m.bp.co.plain.s2": "A breakpoint stops every time execution reaches its line. Inside a loop, that is every iteration. [[src:jb-breakpoints]]",
  "track.debugging.m.bp.co.plain.s3": "The All policy suspends every thread when any thread hits the breakpoint; Thread suspends only that thread. [[src:jb-breakpoints]]",
  "track.debugging.m.bp.co.cond.s1": "The condition is evaluated on every hit; if it is not true, the breakpoint is ignored. The expression must be valid at the breakpoint's line. [[src:jb-breakpoints]]",
  "track.debugging.m.bp.co.cond.s2": "Put the condition on the symptom (a negative fee) rather than on an index: you do not need to know which booking is bad, the debugger finds it.",
  "track.debugging.m.bp.co.cond.s3": "This is a side effect of debugging itself: suspending every thread breaks anything that depends on time, such as heartbeats or network timeouts.",
  "track.debugging.m.bp.co.thread.s1": "Choose the policy by your question: for a frozen snapshot of the whole app, All; to keep the app running around the thread you are looking at, Thread. [[src:jb-breakpoints]]",
  "track.debugging.m.bp.co.thread.s2": "The variables view is a snapshot of the stopped thread: local variables, parameters and object fields, in the frame (function) where it stopped. [[src:jb-examine]]",
  "track.debugging.m.bp.co.thread.s3": "With other threads still running, shared values can change under you. A multithreading bug sometimes vanishes when every thread is stopped and shows up when only one is.",
  "track.debugging.m.bp.co.logbp.s1": "A non-suspending breakpoint is for logging, or as a trigger for another breakpoint. \"Evaluate and log\" writes the result of any expression, evaluated in the context of that line. [[src:jb-breakpoints]]",
  "track.debugging.m.bp.co.logbp.s2": "This replaces a temporary Log.d: the log line lives in the debugger, not in the code, so it cannot slip into a release.",
  "track.debugging.m.bp.co.logbp.s3": "Logging on every iteration still slows the loop a lot compared with running undebugged; do not trust timings taken while the debugger is attached.",
  "track.debugging.vz.tab.bp": "Thread lanes and variables",
